# Keep design.md Current

When making changes that affect the project's architecture, update `design.md` to reflect them. This includes:

- Adding, removing, or renaming CLI commands in `cmd/`
- Adding, removing, or renaming packages under `internal/`
- Changing the `DataSource` interface or `DataItem` struct in `internal/source/source.go`
- Adding new data sources under `internal/source/`
- Changing the cache schema in `internal/cache/cache.go`
- Changing config structure in `internal/config/config.go`
- Switching LLM providers or modifying the LLM client interface in `internal/llm/`

When updating `design.md`:

- Keep the mermaid diagrams accurate (architecture, sequence, class)
- DO NOT add any overview of file structure, this is redundant
- Update the command reference table if commands changed
- Update the cache schema table if columns changed
- Keep descriptions concise; this is a quick-reference design doc, not prose
